options_to_test:
Not an order, a test of what would make Row 2 pass on this brief's terms. On my rebuild, our own share of the bill would have to fall to:
- about 36% to reach zero in S1 (partners near 64%, about $1.9B more than the $4.5B shown);
- about 45% to stay within -5 yp in S3 (Felipe's leg 3);
- about 34% to stay within the Board's -2 yp downside in S3;
- about 17% to clear the +5 yp override margin.
The brief shows none of these. No credit. I want Felipe's and Arjan's reading of whether anything else in the brief moves the row: the line, demand, or tariffs.

